{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Then</b> — Rabbi Marinus said: David speaks on behalf of the congregation of Israel, and this alludes to what our fathers said at Sinai: 'we will do and we will hear.' But the correct interpretation in my eyes: he says this on his own behalf, for in his time of distress he vowed a vow, instructed that it be written down, that he would sing a new song, and now I have come to fulfill the vow. And it is correct that the vow is to do, and this is all my desire."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:21.924376411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}